Consent Management
===================
Checking the Consent Documents
-------------------------------

Castellum is mainly intended for the management of recruitment consents. Study
consents must be obtained separately from the respective study conducters.

1. Log in to Castellum by using your username and password

   - Make sure you are connected to the WiFi and use your right username and
     password
     
2. Click on **Consent documents** and then on **Admin** on the front page

3. Scroll all the way down and press **Consent documents**
   
   - You will see a list of all consent documents that have been created
   - Additional information that will be shown to you: date of creation and
     whether the consent document is valid or not
     
Updating the Consent Documents
-------------------------------

It is possible for a consent document to become invalid because of 
- a change in the legislation
- a present date on which the validity expires
- ...

A) There are two options you may implement when a consent document becomes invalid
   To see the options, go to **Admin** on the front page > **Consent documents**
   in the last section **SUBJECTS** > click on the date the consent document
   you want to change the status for has been created
   
1. The consent form can be marked as **Is deprecated** and **Is valid**
   - This can be considered as an intermediate step between the validity and
     invalidity of a consent document
   - The subjects may remain in the database and may be recruited but a a new
     consent document should be obtained soon
     
2. If you uncheck the box saying **Is valid**, the consent document is marked as
   invalid
   - If the invalidity of the consent is saved, there is no longer any consent
     for the recruitment of a test person in the database
This does not apply when the **Legal basis for data processing** is a **Study
consent** or **Guardianship**. You can see the legal basis for data processing
for each subject individually, if you select a person and go to the tab
**Overview**



B) If you wish to upload a consent document that is currently valid, proceed as
